From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Trevor Gamblin <tgamblin@baylibre.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:31:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] platform: spacemit: k3: Only enable CCI snoops for mapped
 clusters

PLAT_CCI_MAP only has entries for the four CPU clusters (masters 0-3),
but spacemit_k3 calls cci_enable_snoop_dvm_reqs() for masters 0-6.
For masters 4-6, cci_enable_snoop_dvm_reqs() indexes past the end of
cci_slave_if_map[] and writes to an address derived from whatever data
follows it. On QEMU's spacemit-k3 machine this raises a store access
fault early in cold boot, before the console is up, and the boot hart
silently ends up in sbi_hart_hang().

Drop the calls for the unmapped masters, matching the workaround in
the QEMU spacemit-k3 machine documentation.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Trevor Gamblin <tgamblin@baylibre.com>
---
 platform/generic/spacemit/spacemit_k3.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/platform/generic/spacemit/spacemit_k3.c b/platform/generic/spacemit/spacemit_k3.c
index e6f81fb..5a5acbd 100644
--- a/platform/generic/spacemit/spacemit_k3.c
+++ b/platform/generic/spacemit/spacemit_k3.c
@@ -157,9 +157,6 @@ static int spacemit_k3_early_init(bool cold_boot, const void *fdt, const struct
 		cci_enable_snoop_dvm_reqs(1);
 		cci_enable_snoop_dvm_reqs(2);
 		cci_enable_snoop_dvm_reqs(3);
-		cci_enable_snoop_dvm_reqs(4);
-		cci_enable_snoop_dvm_reqs(5);
-		cci_enable_snoop_dvm_reqs(6);
 
 		for (i = 0; i < platform.hart_count; ++i)
 			/* devote the cluster */
